In the Cartesian coordinate system, the origin coincides with the pole of the polar coordinate system, and the positive $x$-axis is the polar axis. The line $l$ passes through the point $P(-1,1)$, and its slope angle is $\alpha=\frac{5\pi}{6}$. The polar equation of the curve $C$ is $\rho=4\sin\theta$.
(I) Find the parametric equation of line $l$ and the Cartesian equation of curve $C$;
(II) Suppose line $l$ intersects curve $C$ at points $A$ and $B$. Find the value of $\overrightarrow{PA}\cdot\overrightarrow{PB}$.

A beverage company has hired a new employee and is conducting a test to determine their salary level. The company has prepared 8 cups of two different beverages, all of the same color, with 4 cups of beverage A and 4 cups of beverage B. The employee is required to taste each cup and select 4 cups of beverage A. If all 4 selections are correct, the monthly salary will be 3500 yuan; if 3 out of 4 selections are correct, the monthly salary will be 2800 yuan, otherwise, the monthly salary will be 2100 yuan. Let X represent the number of correct selections of beverage A by the employee. Assume that the employee has no ability to distinguish between beverages A and B.
(1) Find the probability distribution of X;
(2) Find the expected monthly salary of this employee.

